1
00:00:03,800 --> 00:00:06,762
Here's a small lending protocol: a pool,

2
00:00:06,802 --> 00:00:10,423
a collateral token, an A M M, and a price oracle.

3
00:00:10,463 --> 00:00:12,180
Lenders supply USDC,

4
00:00:12,220 --> 00:00:15,499
and borrowers post WGLD as collateral.

5
00:00:16,099 --> 00:00:19,334
The pool values that collateral through the oracle,

6
00:00:19,374 --> 00:00:22,484
and the oracle just reads the A M M's spot price.

7
00:00:22,524 --> 00:00:25,835
A bug like that only shows up across contracts.

8
00:00:26,435 --> 00:00:27,666
We start a campaign.

9
00:00:27,706 --> 00:00:30,692
The harness has already seeded the whole deployed

10
00:00:30,732 --> 00:00:33,355
protocol into the agent's simulation world,

11
00:00:33,395 --> 00:00:37,195
with code, storage, and balances at their real addresses.

12
00:00:37,795 --> 00:00:39,398
The agent reads the source,

13
00:00:39,438 --> 00:00:42,098
writes a threat model, and starts a campaign:

14
00:00:42,138 --> 00:00:44,036
actors, actions in attack order,

15
00:00:44,076 --> 00:00:46,421
and the properties that must hold.

16
00:00:47,021 --> 00:00:48,720
Each round, the app hands the

17
00:00:48,760 --> 00:00:50,632
agent a batch of call sequences.

18
00:00:50,672 --> 00:00:52,660
It replays them in the simulation,

19
00:00:52,700 --> 00:00:55,947
and every property is checked against the results.

20
00:00:56,547 --> 00:00:59,808
Under the tool calls, every runtime event is kept:

21
00:00:59,848 --> 00:01:02,526
statuses, balance changes, probe outputs.

22
00:01:02,566 --> 00:01:04,598
Any result can be audited.

23
00:01:05,198 --> 00:01:07,532
The chat shows what the agent was told:

24
00:01:07,572 --> 00:01:09,252
the world is already seeded,

25
00:01:09,292 --> 00:01:12,075
so it never deploys or edits code itself.

26
00:01:14,184 --> 00:01:15,137
Then it lands.

27
00:01:15,177 --> 00:01:19,040
The agent buys WGLD to pump the spot price, deposits it,

28
00:01:19,080 --> 00:01:22,415
and borrows far more than the collateral is worth.

29
00:01:22,455 --> 00:01:24,532
The app cuts the trace to three

30
00:01:24,572 --> 00:01:26,907
calls and reproduces it twice.
